/-!
# Constructibility of the ordinary proper exceptional adjoint

Finite coefficient rings `O_E / ell^r O_E` used for the preservation of constructibility by the
ordinary proper exceptional adjoint on the unbounded small étale derived categories.

## Implementation details

The quotient uses the recorded ring of integers and Mathlib's principal-ideal quotient, rather
than replacing `ell` by a uniformizer. Constructibility uses the finite-stratification
predicate; on Noetherian schemes it agrees with the affine-local notion of constructible
étale modules.

## References

* Zheng, *Six operations and Lefschetz--Verdier formula for Deligne--Mumford stacks*,
  Propositions 3.16(2) and 2.29(2).
* Bhatt--Scholze, *The pro-étale topology for schemes*, Lemma 6.7.18.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory

namespace Padic

/-- The quotient `O_E / ell^r O_E` of the ring of integers of `E` by the principal ideal
generated by `ell ^ r`. -/
abbrev coefficientExtensionEllQuotient (ell : ℕ) [Fact ell.Prime]
    (E : Type v) [Field E] [Algebra ℚ_[ell] E] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[ell] E] (r : ℕ) :=
  coefficientExtensionIntegers ell E ⧸
    Ideal.span ({(ell : coefficientExtensionIntegers ell E) ^ r} :
      Set (coefficientExtensionIntegers ell E))

end Padic

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Etale

end AlgebraicGeometry.Etale
